Negative control for the cell being drawn by the renderer its `type` NAMES
(`R6-36`).

Stops the registry asking its testers and answers every declared cell with the
first registered entry instead. This is the pre-ruling shape wearing the new
clothes: the element list still names `TableCellDate` / `TableCellIcon` /
`TableCellBadges`, the registry still holds four entries with four testers, and
every cell nonetheless comes out as text — which is what a surface resolving by
position rather than by tester does. Nothing is disabled and nothing throws, so
only the dispatch law is on trial.

Re-pointed for `R7-2`: the resolution moved out of `CellDispatcher` into
`cells.renderers`, where the frame reads it too, so the control mutates the ONE
resolution rather than the dispatcher's former copy of it.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the cell-renderer spec — a `TableCellIcon` element no longer draws its
glyph, a `TableCellBadges` element draws no badges, and a `TableCellDate`
element stops speaking its relative form, so every per-type case fails while the
text case still passes.

